      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Al Barqy, from <span class=\"iTxt\">Sa’a</span>d Bin <span class=\"iTxt\">Sa’a</span>d, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Al-Hassan Al-Reza<sup>asws</sup>, said, ‘I asked him<sup>asws</sup> about the one in <span class=\"iTxt\">Ihraam</span>, ‘Can he buy the slave girl, and sell?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Yes’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "8. Ahmad ibn Muhammad has narrated from al-Barqiy from Sa‘d ibn Sa‘d who has said the following: “I once asked abu al-Hassan, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about a man who is in the state of Ihram; if he can buy and sell slave-girls. He (the Imam) said, ‘Yes, he can do so.” "
        ]
      }
